@server1 = http://localhost:5001
@server2 = http://localhost:5002

### Step 1 - Login on Server1: creates a session in Server1's in-memory cache
# @name login
POST {{server1}}/login?user=hasib

### Step 2a - Profile on the SAME server (Server1): works, session is found
GET {{server1}}/profile?sessionId={{login.response.body.sessionId}}

### Step 2b - Profile on a DIFFERENT server (Server2): broken, session not found (401)
### This is the broken state: in-memory cache is per-instance, so Server2 never saw the login.
### Fix: use a distributed cache (e.g. Redis) so that all instances share the same session state.
GET {{server2}}/profile?sessionId={{login.response.body.sessionId}}

###
